        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>SPECTRAL PRISON</strong></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>THE NIGHTMARE IS REMEMBERING. BREAK THE LOOP.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You wake up in a suffocatingly familiar room. You have no memories only a cold, absolute certainty that you have walked these floorboards a thousand times before. Something terrible happened here, and the house won’t let you leave until you remember what it was.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Spectral Prison</i> is a dense, 1-hour psychological horror experience. Reality is a hand-crafted trap, and your only way out is to navigate a repeating cycle that warps around your actions.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>THE RULES OF RECOVERY:</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Uncanny Safe Haven:</strong> The central house cannot kill you, but it will break your mind. The horror is atmospheric and scripted—walls vanish when your back is turned, objects move on their own, and familiar rooms suddenly render completely upside down.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Lethal Extraction Zones:</strong> Safety ends at the end of each loop. To progress, you must plunge into hostile outer locales to hunt down vital story keys. In these zones, <strong>The Warden</strong> is actively hunting you. If you are caught, you die.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Troll Room Gauntlet:</strong> Integrated into every single loop is a psychological choke point. You are trapped in a room flooded with hundreds of deceptive, counterfeit keys. You must master the spatial rules, keep your head, and isolate the one true path to advance.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Natural Atmosphere Over Cheap Scares:</strong> No artificial jump-scares or flashing lights. Every ringing phone, shifting corridor, and surreal layout change is meticulously designed to build pure, natural dread as the truth of your past begins to unravel.</p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>SPECTRAL PRISON</strong></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>THE NIGHTMARE IS REMEMBERING. BREAK THE LOOP.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You wake up in a suffocatingly familiar room. You have no memories only a cold, absolute certainty that you have walked these floorboards a thousand times before. Something terrible happened here, and the house won’t let you leave until you remember what it was.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Spectral Prison</i> is a dense, 1-hour psychological horror experience. Reality is a hand-crafted trap, and your only way out is to navigate a repeating cycle that warps around your actions.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>THE RULES OF RECOVERY:</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Uncanny Safe Haven:</strong> The central house cannot kill you, but it will break your mind. The horror is atmospheric and scripted—walls vanish when your back is turned, objects move on their own, and familiar rooms suddenly render completely upside down.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Lethal Extraction Zones:</strong> Safety ends at the end of each loop. To progress, you must plunge into hostile outer locales to hunt down vital story keys. In these zones, <strong>The Warden</strong> is actively hunting you. If you are caught, you die.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Troll Room Gauntlet:</strong> Integrated into every single loop is a psychological choke point. You are trapped in a room flooded with hundreds of deceptive, counterfeit keys. You must master the spatial rules, keep your head, and isolate the one true path to advance.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Natural Atmosphere Over Cheap Scares:</strong> No artificial jump-scares or flashing lights. Every ringing phone, shifting corridor, and surreal layout change is meticulously designed to build pure, natural dread as the truth of your past begins to unravel.</p></li></ul>",
        "short_description": "Escape a prison that rewrites itself with every loop. Search a shifting house where keys never spawn in the same place, survive the Warden's deadly game zones, and unravel a haunting personal horror in this psychological thriller. How many runs will it take to break the cycle?",
